/// Owner-scoped power arms must compare `cleared` against
/// [`owner_of_listener`]: C# `BlockNextTurnPower.AfterBlockCleared(creature)`
/// (and `SelfFormingClayPower`) gate on `creature == base.Owner`, so the
/// power's block-regrant fires ONLY when the OWNER's block clears — not on
/// every creature's turn-start clear. `cleared == None` (the [`Default`])
/// means "unspecified" and never matches an owner, so default-constructed
/// test/placeholder contexts no longer fire those arms; tests that exercise
/// the player turn-start clear pass `Some(CreatureRef::Player)` explicitly.
/// Bead `sts2-rs-2e9q2` follow-up.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default)]
pub struct BlockClearedCtx {
    pub cleared: Option<CreatureRef>,
}

